  "id": "COMPOUND:2827 - PROTEIN:3764",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which Quisqualic acid may interact with Telomerase-binding protein EST1A, through a series of target-mediated pathways. Quisqualic acid is implicated in targeting 5-oxoprolinase, which in turn is a target of D-Aspartic Acid and D-Glutamic Acid. These compounds are all involved in the regulation of Telomerase-binding protein EST1A, indicating a possible convergent pathway where Quisqualic acid may act through a shared intermediate, 5-oxoprolinase, to influence the function of EST1A. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a plausible biological link, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction between Quisqualic acid and EST1A.",
